                            <comment id="16702493" author="tagar" created="Wed, 28 Nov 2018 23:02:58 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Here&apos;s a very interesting thread how a very popular `event-stream` npm package got hacked&#160;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/dominictarr/event-stream/issues/116&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://github.com/dominictarr/event-stream/issues/116&lt;/a&gt;&#160;&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16702500" author="derektapley" created="Wed, 28 Nov 2018 23:09:16 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;I was able to successfully build again, here are the steps I took:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Navigate to ./zeppelin-web&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Open package-lock.json in the editor of your choice&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Navigate down to the event-stream dependency (as of commit &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/apache/zeppelin/commit/d1606c248d4398d929683de284c62d630d19806c&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;d1606c2&lt;/a&gt;, this is on line 4523)&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Bump version to 4.0.1&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;In the requires section, remove &quot;flatmap-stream&quot;: &quot;^0.1.0&quot;,&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Save package-lock.json&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Verify fix with npm install --no-lock&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;


&lt;p&gt;This should fix the problem with flatmap-stream being removed from npmjs.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
